# Re-applies only the rig files onto an already-built image.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. A full rebuild re-runs `chmod -R a+rX` over the Rust toolchain and
# cargo registry, which on overlayfs copies up the entire tree into a new layer. Once
# Docker Desktop garbage-collects the build cache -- measured going from 15.53GB
# reclaimable to 2.04GB between attempts -- that step has to run again, and on a 15.7GB
# machine it was killed for low memory eight times running, at every headroom from
# 0.8GB to 8.5GB free and with the WSL VM capped at both 6GB and 4GB. It is not a cost
# that can be made room for.
#
# It is also unnecessary. The rig files below are the ONLY things that change between
# most iterations, they are plain COPYs at the end of the real Dockerfile, and the
# product tarball is verifiably untouched -- `COPY thol/pkg/optimizer.tgz` reports
# CACHED. So the base image is reused and only these are re-applied.
#
# The provenance file comes along deliberately: an image whose entrypoint and manifests
# are newer than its provenance record is exactly the unattributable build this rig
# refuses to run. Rebuild from thol/Dockerfile whenever anything under src/ changes.
FROM thol-rig:local

# THE MOUNTPOINT HAS TO EXIST IN THE IMAGE, OWNED BY THE RUNTIME USER. Docker seeds a
# fresh named volume from the image path it is mounted at -- content and ownership. The
# image had no /results at all, so Docker created the mountpoint as root:root, the
# container runs as bench, and the entrypoint's `[ -w /results ]` guard then skipped
# persistence: four runs completed, nothing was recorded, and the next attempt re-paid
# for them.
#
# `thol-results` escaped this only by accident of age -- it already existed, bench-owned,
# from an earlier image. Any NEW volume reproduced the fault, which is what made it look
# like the nested `-v graph:/results/proxy-graph` mount was to blame. It was not: an
# unnested mount of a fresh volume fails identically. Verified both ways.
# root only for this one step: the base image ends as `bench`, which cannot mkdir in /.
USER root
RUN mkdir -p /results && chown bench:bench /results
USER bench

COPY thol/pkg/provenance.json /opt/optimizer-provenance.json
COPY --chown=bench:bench thol/entrypoint.sh /home/bench/scripts/entrypoint.sh
COPY --chown=bench:bench thol/manifests/ /home/bench/manifests/
